title: Choosing Our Enemies
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1922 and enemies_timer <= 0
on-arrival: week_actions += 1; enemies_timer = 9
max-visits: 8
is-card: true
card-image: img/Enemies.jpg
tags: party_affairs

= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @anti_dem: The anti-democratic parties of the far right and left - the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span>, and the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">[+ pnf_name +]</span>.
- @communists: The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span> alone.
- @pnf: The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">[+ pnf_name +]</span> alone.
- @religious: The Religious parties - the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span>.
- @bourgeois: The <span style="color:#0047AB;">Bou</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">rge</span><span style="color:#1E99C5;">ois</span> parties - the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#FFD700;">[+ ldr_name +]</span> and <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#0047AB;">[+ ul_name +]</span>.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@anti_dem
view-if: pcdi_formed
on-arrival: enemies = "anti-democratic parties"; maximalist_strength += 5; reformist_strength += 5; communist_dissent += 5; workers_pcdi -= 2; workers_pnf -= 2; radicalisation -= 0.05;

Attacking the far right and left is popular among all but the left wing of our party, who would prefer to be fighting the <span style="color:#0047AB;">bou</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">rge</span><span style="color:#1E99C5;">ois</span> parties.

@communists
view-if: pcdi_formed
on-arrival: enemies = "PCd'I"; reformist_strength += 5; communist_dissent += 8; reformist_dissent -= 5; pcdi_relation -= 15; ldr_relation += 3; ul_relation += 5; ppi_relation += 5; workers_pcdi -= 4; radicalisation -= 0.05;

Attacking the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span> is supported by all but the most left-wing <span style="color:#ED2855">socialists</span>, and wins us some measure of approval among the <span style="color:#0047AB;">bou</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">rge</span><span style="color:#1E99C5;">ois</span> parties. However, If we are to reconcile with the <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span>, this may not be the best choice.

@pnf
on-arrival: enemies = pnf_name; fasci_urgency += 1; workers_pnf -= 4; nationalist_sentiment -= 3*(1-dissent); workers_pnf += 4 if pnf_votes < 2; veterans_pnf += 8 if pnf_votes < 2

[? if (fasci_urgency == 0 or pnf_seating_disp < 10) and prime_minister_party != pnf_name : The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">[+ pnf_name +]</span> is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. ?][? if (fasci_urgency > 0 and pnf_seating_disp >= 10) or prime_minister_party == pnf_name : The <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">fascists</span> are the most urgent problem for us to deal with. ?][? if pnf_votes < 2 and not pnf_in_government : Worse, giving them attention while they're such a small party only attracts attention to them. ?]

@religious
on-arrival: enemies = "religious parties"; communist_strength += 5; reformist_dissent += 8; communist_dissent -= 5; ppi_relation -= 15; workers_ppi -= 4; republican_sentiment -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if socialist_catholic_coalition

Attacking the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span> certainly aligns with our secular ideals, and wins us some measure of approval among the left. However, it may make it harder to build the coalitions that are necessary for government in the future.

@bourgeois
on-arrival: enemies = "bourgeois parties"; left_strength += 8; left_dissent -= 5; ldr_relation -= 5; ul_relation -= 5; reformist_dissent += 8; workers_ldr -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1 if centre_left_coalition; republican_sentiment -= 3

Our anti-<span style="color:#0047AB;">bou</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">rge</span><span style="color:#1E99C5;">ois</span> rhetoric is popular among the left, but may make it harder to build the coalitions that are necessary for government in the future.
